	(tokenizer_type_SentencePieceTokenizer | tokenizer_type_GPTSentencePieceTokenizer | tokenizer_type_Llama2Tokenizer | tokenizer_type_TikTokenizer | tokenizer_type_HuggingFaceTokenizer | tokenizer_type_MultimodalTokenizer | tokenizer_type_SFTTokenizer) => tokenizer_model
	// build_tokenizer.py:79-82 MultimodalTokenizer reads args.tokenizer_prompt_format, which only examples/multimodal/multimodal_args.py:120 registers (an entry point of its own); with pretrain_gpt.py: "'Namespace' object has no attribute 'tokenizer_prompt_format'". Attempt 28 mut_502. At runtime
	tokenizer_type_MultimodalTokenizer => entry_point_other
	// ===== v30: rules from Experiment 2 attempt 28 (model v27, plain image) =====
	// fused_a2a.py:611-668 the flex dispatcher's ncclep backend bootstraps TE's NCCL EP with te_ep.ep_bootstrap(..., num_topk=...); TE 2.18's ep_bootstrap has no num_topk parameter (it was added in TE 2.19), so with TE 2.18 ("ep_bootstrap() got an unexpected keyword argument 'num_topk'") the backend cannot start. Megatron checks only that the module exists. Attempt 28 valid_0000 (plain image, EP 4); signatures checked in both images. v36: only when a forward pass runs, i.e. training or validation (training.py:6065: --full-validation or eval_iters > 0); attempt 34 mut_507 escaped with --skip-train and --eval-iters 0. v45: the effective backend: --moe-enable-deepep turns ncclep into deepep before any check reads it (transformer_config.py:2110-2115; held-out attempt 41 valid_1518). At runtime
	((num_experts & num_experts != 0) & moe_token_dispatcher_type_flex & (moe_flex_dispatcher_backend_ncclep & !moe_enable_deepep) & ((!skip_train & ((train_iters & train_iters != 0) | (train_samples & train_samples != 0))) | full_validation | eval_iters > 0)) => platform_te_version >= 219
	// ===== v31: rules from Experiment 2 attempt 29 (model v29, full image v2) =====
	// fused_a2a.py:318-345 + DeepEP hybrid_ep/config.cuh:86-101/174-185 HybridEPBuffer rejects its buffer config unless (local experts x ranks per node) % 4 == 0 (also hidden % 16, or % 512 with fp8 dispatch); for a single-node TP x EP group that is (num_experts / EP) x (TP x EP) = num_experts x TP ('The buffer config is not valid.'). Attempt 29 valid_0037 and a bisection on GPUs 5-6 (2 experts: EP 1 + CP 2, EP 2, EP 2 without paged stash all fail). At model build
	((num_experts & num_experts != 0) & moe_token_dispatcher_type_flex & moe_flex_dispatcher_backend_hybridep) => num_experts * tensor_model_parallel_size == aux_div_hybridep * 4
	// [aux-def] auxiliary multiplier aux_div_hybridep is a positive integer
	aux_div_hybridep >= 1
	// ===== v32: rules from Experiment 2 attempt 30 (model v30, plain image) =====
	// moe_layer.py:690-694 MoELayer.forward raises in training mode when its attention TP group (pg_collection.tp) has more than one rank and sequence parallelism is off ('During training, performance may degrade if MoE and tensor parallelism are enabled without also enabling sequence parallelism.'). Nothing earlier enforces it: ModelParallelConfig only warns, and only for EP > 1, and validate_args switches sequence parallelism off for TP 1 only. Attempt 30 mut_507 (TP 2, flex/ncclep) stopped here before the TE check it targeted. At runtime
	((num_experts & num_experts != 0) & tensor_model_parallel_size > 1 & !skip_train & ((train_iters & train_iters != 0) | (train_samples & train_samples != 0))) => sequence_parallel
	// [aux-def] transformer_config.py:1041 + 1634-1635 effective value: moe_router_aux_loss_fusion defaults to None, which follows moe_router_fusion, and the CLI can only turn it off (--no-moe-router-aux-loss-fusion); so it is true only when moe_router_fusion is (attempt 30 mut_150 could not be mapped without this)
	moe_router_aux_loss_fusion => moe_router_fusion
	// ===== v33: rules from Experiment 2 attempt 31 (model v31, full image v2) =====
	// transformer_config.py:2836-2848 with the embedding and/or the loss counted in the pipeline split and no effective VPP, (num_layers + embedding + loss) must be divisible by PP. --num-virtual-stages-per-pipeline-rank 1 leaves no effective VPP, a case that neither the VPP-unset rules (constraints_v6_divisibility.uvl) nor the VPP != 1 rules (constraints_v12_coverage.uvl) cover. Attempt 31 valid_0693 (PP 4, 8 layers + embedding, VPP 1: 'number of middle layers: 9 must be divisible by middle pipeline_model_parallel_size 4')
